LeetCode #30 — Substring with Concatenation of All Words
Difficulty: Hard
Language: C++
Problem:
Given a string s and an array of strings words, where all words have the same length, find all starting indices of substrings in s that contain every word from words exactly once and without any intervening characters.
The order of the words does not matter.
Example:
Input:  s = "barfoothefoobarman"
        words = ["foo","bar"]

Output: [0,9]
Explanation:
The substrings "barfoo" and "foobar" contain both "bar" and "foo" exactly once.
Constraints:
1 <= s.length <= 10⁴
1 <= words.length <= 5000
1 <= words[i].length <= 30
All words[i] have the same length.
